# Norway's priority-setting system, criterion by criterion
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical","b":"gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical"}
next: {"title":"Whose costs count? The perspective question decides the answer","href":"https://drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/dcast/health-technology-assessment-deciding/whose-costs-count-the-perspective.cast"}

## Two Answers, One Drug
voice: female
level: basic
use: timeline
with:
    title: Nusinersen (Spinraza) in Norway
    start_label: '2017'
    end_label: '2018'
    milestones:
      - {label: Approved in Europe, sublabel: '2017'}
      - {label: Method assessment, sublabel: DMP}
      - {label: 'No', sublabel: 'Beslutningsforum, 2017', emphasize: true}
      - {label: Price negotiation, sublabel: confidential}
      - {label: 'Yes, under 18', sublabel: February 2018, emphasize: true}

    box n_nytte "Nytte (benefit)" #2f6b8f hidden true
    box n_ressurs "Ressursbruk (resource use)" #b5482e hidden true
    box n_alvor "Alvorlighet (severity)" #8a5fa8 hidden true
    box n_dec "Yes / No" hidden true
    arrow a_n n_nytte -> n_dec #2f6b8f hidden true
    arrow a_r n_ressurs -> n_dec #b5482e hidden true
    arrow a_a n_alvor -> n_dec #8a5fa8 hidden true

Across this series we take Norway's priority-setting system apart criterion by criterion — starting with one drug file that got two opposite answers.
    draw line title

Nusinersen, sold as Spinraza, was licensed in Europe in 2017: the first drug ever approved for spinal muscular atrophy, whose severest form kills most infants, or leaves them permanently ventilated, before their second birthday.
    draw dot_0 label_0

    pause 0.3

The medicines agency, then called Legemiddelverket, ran the method assessment — how much health the drug buys, and what it costs to buy it.
    draw dot_1 label_1

At its US list price — around 750 000 dollars in the first year and about 375 000 every year after — the cost per QALY came out many times above the values Norway works with.
    point at.ref dot_1 gesture tap

So in 2017 Beslutningsforum said no — not because the drug fails, the trial effect was real, but because of the health that price would take from patients we never see.
    draw dot_2 label_2

    pause 0.4

Then the manufacturer and the health trusts negotiated; the Norwegian price is confidential, but it is lower.
    draw dot_3 label_3

February 2018: yes — for patients who begin treatment before they turn eighteen.
    draw dot_4 label_4

Same drug, same trials, four months apart: no, then yes with an age limit.
    camera center.ref dot_3 zoom 1.7 delivery grave

    camera reset true

Any rule Norway claims to follow has to be able to produce both of these.
    highlight dot_2 dot_4 effect glow

    pause 0.5

    clear

The rule is written down, in the 2015–16 white paper Meld. St. 34: three criteria. First, nytte — benefit, the QALYs a technology is expected to add.
    draw n_nytte

Second, ressursbruk — resource use: everything the health service must spend to get those QALYs.
    draw n_ressurs

Third, alvorlighet — severity: how much is at stake for these patients if we do nothing.
    draw n_alvor

And severity is turned into a number — absolutt prognosetap, the absolute shortfall: the QALYs a patient loses compared with a healthy person of the same age.
    label lbl_shortfall "Absolutt prognosetap: QALYs lost vs. a healthy peer" below #8a5fa8 attach_to n_alvor

The larger that shortfall, the more we accept paying per QALY — from a reference around 275 000 kroner up to roughly three times that at the highest severity.
    label lbl_lambda "275 000 → 825 000 kr/QALY" right #8a5fa8 attach_to n_alvor

All three enter a single yes or no — and for an infant with SMA type one, the shortfall is close to an entire lifetime.
    draw n_dec a_n a_r a_a

That judgement also has an address: Bestillerforum orders the assessment, the Directorate for Medical Products writes it, Beslutningsforum — the four regional directors — decides; outpatient drugs travel the separate blåresept route.
    point at.ref n_dec gesture circle

So nusinersen's two answers were not a contradiction: benefit and severity never moved, the price did — and the same rule turned over.
    mark mark_dec target n_dec kind box

Next: the three criteria one at a time, then severity as a number, then who actually decides, and finally the four commissions — Lønning I, Lønning II, Norheim and Magnussen — that built this machinery.

## Nytte, Ressursbruk, Alvorlighet
voice: female
level: basic
use: cost_effectiveness_plane
with:
    title: 'Meld. St. 34 (2015–2016): three criteria, one judgement'
    x_label: 'nytte: ΔE (QALYs)'
    y_label: 'ressursbruk: ΔC (kr)'
    wtp_threshold: 275000
    quadrant_labels: true
    points:
      - {label: Hip replacement, effect: 2, cost: 120000}
      - {label: 'New drug, severe disease', effect: 0.4, cost: 180000, emphasize: true}

One drug got two different answers, and the rulebook behind both is the three criteria of Meld. St. 34, Norway's priority white paper of 2015 to 2016.
    draw x_axis

The first criterion is nytte — benefit — how much health a technology adds: our ΔE, measured in QALYs.
    point at.ref x_axis gesture underline

The second is ressursbruk — resource use — what it consumes: ΔC, in kroner.
    draw y_axis

    draw q_ne q_nw q_se q_sw parallel true

    pause 0.3

A hip replacement lands far out here: roughly a couple of good years for around a hundred thousand kroner. Placements on this plane are illustrative, but the order of magnitude is real.
    draw pt_0 pt_label_0

    pause 0.3

And here a drug for a severe, rare disease: 0.4 QALYs per patient for 180,000 kroner more — about 450,000 kroner per QALY.
    draw pt_1 pt_label_1

Neither number decides alone. The pair is read against a line through the origin whose slope is lambda, our willingness to pay per QALY — the white paper's illustrative figure was 275,000 kroner for a good life year.
    draw wtp_line wtp_label

The drug sits above that line. On nytte and ressursbruk alone, the answer is no.
    highlight pt_1 effect glow

    pause 0.4

The third criterion, alvorlighet — severity — is not a third coordinate on this plane. It moves the line.
    label sev_label "alvorlighet (severity) sets the slope λ" above-left #8a5fa8 attach_to wtp_line

The greater the absolute shortfall — the health these patients lose compared with their peers — the more we accept paying, in practice up to about three times as much, roughly 825,000 kroner per QALY.
    animate wtp_threshold 825000 delivery grave duration 3

Same benefit, same cost, same point — and now it lies under the line.
    camera center.ref pt_1 zoom 2

That is what the white paper means by assessing the criteria jointly: what decides is the point against the line, never one number on its own.
    mark mark_accept target pt_1 kind circle

    camera reset true

Severity, though, buys a steeper line — not an unlimited one.
    erase q_ne q_nw q_se q_sw parallel true

Nusinersen, our running example, sits so far up this cost axis that the page cannot hold it: at list price its cost per QALY ran into the millions, even against the highest severity Norway recognises.
    highlight y_axis effect glow

Beslutningsforum said no in 2017, and yes in February 2018 for patients under eighteen — once the price had moved.

    pause 0.4

Three criteria, one judgement: nytte and ressursbruk place the point, alvorlighet sets the line, and only the two together give an answer.
    draw title

## Who actually decides
voice: female
level: basic
use: pathway
with:
    title: 'Who actually decides: one assessment, two decision routes'
    edges: Proposal -> Bestillerforum; Bestillerforum -> DMP; DMP -> LIS price talks; LIS price talks -> Beslutningsforum; Beslutningsforum -> Hospital use; Outpatient drug -> DMP; DMP -> Blaresept
    node_types:
      Proposal: protein
      Bestillerforum: gene
      DMP: gene
      LIS price talks: gene
      Beslutningsforum: gene
      Hospital use: protein
      Outpatient drug: protein
      Blaresept: protein

    label conf_label "Negotiated price: confidential" below #b5482e attach_to node_lis_price_talks hidden true
    mark conf_mark target conf_label kind box hidden true

    camera center.x 500 center.y 355 zoom 1.2

Severity, once it is a number, still has to travel through the rooms that turn it into a yes or a no — because in Norway the body that calculates is never the body that decides.
    draw title

Any clinician, company or health trust can propose a method — nusinersen for spinal muscular atrophy entered here in 2017.
    draw node_proposal node_label_proposal

    pause 0.3

Bestillerforum commissions the work, deciding whether a method is assessed at all.
    draw edge_0 node_bestillerforum node_label_bestillerforum

A method never commissioned here simply never reaches a decision.
    point at.ref node_bestillerforum gesture circle

For drugs, the method assessment is written by the Directorate for Medical Products — DMP, called Legemiddelverket until 2024.
    draw edge_1 node_dmp node_label_dmp

Here the three criteria become arithmetic: nytte and ressursbruk collapse into an ICER, alvorlighet into absolutt prognosetap.
    highlight node_dmp effect glow

    pause 0.3

Then Sykehusinnkjøp negotiates a price — and the ICER that counts is computed at that negotiated price, never the list price.
    draw edge_2 node_lis_price_talks node_label_lis_price_talks

Only now does Beslutningsforum decide, for the whole country at once.
    draw edge_3 node_beslutningsforum node_label_beslutningsforum

Four people sit in that room: the chief executives of the four regional health authorities, meeting roughly once a month.
    camera center.ref node_beslutningsforum zoom 1.9 delivery grave

They said no to nusinersen in 2017, then yes in February 2018 at a new price, with an age limit of eighteen years.
    camera center.x 500 center.y 355 zoom 1.2

A yes means every hospital in Norway may use it; a no means none may.
    draw edge_4 node_hospital_use node_label_hospital_use

    pause 0.5

Yet most drugs never meet those four executives — the ones you collect at a pharmacy take another road into the very same agency.
    draw node_outpatient_drug node_label_outpatient_drug edge_5

Blaresept, the blue prescription, is reimbursement from the national insurance scheme — and DMP grants it itself, with no forum at all.
    draw edge_6 node_blaresept node_label_blaresept

Unless the bill would exceed roughly a hundred million kroner a year, when it must go to the Storting with the budget.
    label blar_note "Above ~100 mill. kr per year → Storting" below #8f887c attach_to node_blaresept

Same criteria, same agency doing the sums — but who says yes depends on whether the drug is given in a ward or handed across a counter.
    focus node_dmp node_blaresept node_beslutningsforum

    pause 0.4

And this box is where Norwegian priority setting currently quarrels with itself: the negotiated price is confidential.
    draw conf_label

The published assessment shows list prices, so no outsider can recompute the number the decision actually rested on.
    draw conf_mark

Secrecy is defended as what buys Norway the discount; it also means a public decision leans on a figure the public may not see.
    highlight conf_label effect pulse

Four rooms, one route: whoever calculates does not decide, and whoever decides cannot show you the number.
    delivery grave

## Four Commissions, One System
voice: female
level: basic
domain: {"x":[0,20],"y":[0,900]}
use: timeline
with:
    title: Four commissions, one system
    start_label: '1987'
    end_label: '2016'
    milestones:
      - {label: Lønning I, sublabel: NOU 1987:23}
      - {label: Lønning II, sublabel: NOU 1997:18}
      - {label: Norheim, sublabel: NOU 2014:12}
      - {label: Magnussen, sublabel: '2015'}
      - {label: Meld. St. 34, sublabel: 2015–2016, emphasize: true}

    axes sev_axes x_label "Absolutt prognosetap (QALYs lost)" y_label "Accepted price (1000 kr per QALY)" hidden true
    curve wtp_line #2f6b8f expr "275 + 27.5*x" hidden true
    label label_wtp "Severity buys tolerance for cost" above-left #2f6b8f attach_to wtp_line hidden true
    dot pt_base at.x 0 at.y 275 hidden true
    label label_base "≈ 275 000 kr/QALY" right attach_to pt_base hidden true
    dot pt_top at.x 20 at.y 825 guides true hidden true
    label label_top "≈ 825 000 kr/QALY" above-left attach_to pt_top hidden true
    box n_nytte "Nytte" #2f6b8f hidden true
    box n_alv "Alvorlighet" #8a5fa8 hidden true
    box n_ress "Ressursbruk" #b5482e hidden true
    box n_dec "Yes — under 18" hidden true
    label label_nytte "motor function gained" above #2f6b8f attach_to n_nytte hidden true
    label label_alv "shortfall near the maximum" above #8a5fa8 attach_to n_alv hidden true
    label label_ress "price above even the raised λ" above #b5482e attach_to n_ress hidden true
    edge e1 n_nytte -> n_dec hidden true
    edge e2 n_alv -> n_dec hidden true
    edge e3 n_ress -> n_dec hidden true
    mark mark_dec target n_dec kind box hidden true

Who decides is one question; where their three criteria came from is another — four public commissions across thirty years.
    draw title line

Lønning I, reporting in 1987, was among the first national priority commissions anywhere: it sorted all of Norwegian health care into five levels, ranked by severity alone.
    draw dot_0 label_0

Ten years later Lønning II added expected benefit and a reasonable relation between cost and effect, and its priority groups fed straight into the 1999 Patients' Rights Act.
    draw dot_1 label_1

Norheim's committee in 2014 named three criteria outright: health benefit, resource use, and health loss measured across a whole lifetime.
    draw dot_2 label_2

That last one counted health a patient had already lost, so an eighty-year-old could barely score on it — the hearing responses were fierce, and the criterion did not survive.
    highlight dot_2 label_2 effect glow

So a second group under Jon Magnussen replaced it in 2015 with absolutt prognosetap — the QALYs lost from today forward, not the ones already behind you.
    draw dot_3 label_3

Meld. St. 34 took that to the Storting in 2016, and the three criteria we now work with — nytte, ressursbruk, alvorlighet — became national policy.
    draw dot_4 label_4

    pause 0.5

    clear

Between 1987 and 2015, severity travelled from a rank order to a number — and a number can do something a rank order cannot.
    draw sev_axes

Put absolute shortfall on the horizontal axis and the price we accept per QALY on the vertical: the more future health a condition destroys, the more we are willing to pay to save some of it.
    draw wtp_line label_wtp

The reference figure at ordinary severity has been about 275 000 kroner per QALY; at the extreme end Magnussen's proposal reached roughly 825 000.
    draw pt_base label_base pt_top label_top

Magnussen proposed six discrete severity classes between those ends — the white paper kept the graded logic but left the boundaries to judgement, so this straight line is illustrative, not statutory.
    camera center.ref pt_top zoom 2

    camera reset true

    pause 0.4

    clear

Now run nusinersen through the machinery. Nytte: infants with SMA type 1 who would never have sat unsupported gained motor function — the benefit is real and visible.
    draw n_nytte label_nytte

Alvorlighet: untreated, the condition takes almost an entire expected lifetime, so the absolute prognosis loss sits at the very top of the scale, and lifts the acceptable price with it.
    draw n_alv label_alv

Ressursbruk: at a launch price of several million kroner per patient in the first year, the cost per QALY overshot even that raised ceiling — which is why Beslutningsforum said no in 2017.
    draw n_ress label_ress

In February 2018, after a price agreement and further documentation, the same body said yes — but only for patients under eighteen, where the evidence of benefit was strongest.
    draw e1 e2 e3 n_dec mark_dec

Across these five parts, that is the whole system in one sentence: Norway never decided whether nusinersen was worth it — it decided how to decide, and the age limit is what four commissions, three criteria and one number produced.
    delivery grave

